; A FOURTH THROW POINT AND A FOURTH DIE (COMBAT_LOOP.md C4). Pool size 3 was assumed in five
; places plus this scene (SEAMS.md section 8); the code stopped assuming it in C2 and this is the
; scene catching up. A Nerve adds the Heart die to a pool that does not use it (CORE_RULES.md
; section 7), which makes a genuine fourth solid on the felt - and DiceTray sits it out again for
; every pool that does not want it, so nothing changes for an ordinary three-die swing.
;
; Behind the other three and off to the near side, so the four launch as a spread rather than a
; line: dice that leave the hand on the same arc land on top of each other, which is where most
; cocked landings came from (M2).
[node name="ThrowPoint4" type="Marker3D" parent="ThrowPoints" unique_id=1357251619]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -0.1, 0.26, 0.1)

